id:                     E14859
trigger_tool:           clang|conan|make
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        alsa/seq_event.h file not found|public header includes unexported dependency header
severity:               2
category:               headers,conan,portability,ohos
match_keywords:         private ALSA header,alsa/seq_event.h,alsa/asoundlib.h,public umbrella header,transitive headers
title:                  Repair installed public headers that include private dependency headers
root_cause: An installed library header includes a dependency subheader not supplied by the published dependency package; downstream consumers fail even when the library itself compiled in a richer source tree. Autoconf can select the mksh print builtin while detecting the configure interpreter, then execute config.status under Bash where print does not exist. That breaks generated Libtool contents even though configure returns success. Use a declared Bash tool consistently for configure and generated-helper execution.
affected_scope:         C or C++ libraries whose exported headers include dependency-private paths while the package manager only exposes public headers.
verification_cmd:       Build an installed-package consumer including only the library public header, using the exact published dependency graph, and execute a real API assertion.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           public-umbrella-include-and-transitive-requirements
rec_description: Replace the private include with the dependency public umbrella header, declare the dependency in the recipe, and ensure downstream compile and link metadata exposes the required public headers and libraries. Autoconf can select the mksh print builtin while detecting the configure interpreter, then execute config.status under Bash where print does not exist. That breaks generated Libtool contents even though configure returns success. Use a declared Bash tool consistently for configure and generated-helper execution.
rec_command:            patch exported header include; conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<ohos-profile>; inspect installed-header consumer compile and run
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               public-header-patch-and-real-consumer
forbid_1_pattern:       copy-private-header-into-package
forbid_1_reason:        Vendoring a dependency-private header freezes an unsupported ABI and hides the missing public dependency contract.
forbid_1_consequence:   A future dependency update can compile with mismatched declarations or break downstream consumers.
principles:             []
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E14859-draft-2501.md
last_updated: 2026-10-13
source_event: dssi/1.1.1 exported dssi.h include patch; OHOS W3 dssi-w3-20261004T043844Z upstream Automake 1/1 and installed consumer 1/1; raw log SHA-256 8403f4e9ba990c4259527505da01bf70d7cf6c78bebdae0d830ebcfa1a99d9082. 2026-10-13 current CI repair; dssi-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r2, official CI log SHA256 d2b51f0f9ab024025676c7bb4d7466940ccfc8e7756172a96207952c0d64ed7a; The earlier native tuple/header closure does not prove generator interpreter consistency. Diagnose print failures before the later Libtool syntax error; do not rewrite generated Libtool, insert fake print commands, or add -fcommon/compiler relaxations.
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-10-04
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         2501
ci_tmpdir_increment:    Public header/helper closure is not generated-file writability: a compiler-proven native tuple and the correct published dependency headers can both pass while config.status retains mktemp-d mode0700 and fallback umask077. Keep these independent contracts rather than enlarging include paths or changing dependency versions to repair a filesystem failure.
ci_tmpdir_repair:       OHOS-only strict three release anchors; both mkdir branches under umask007 in a fresh build-private TMPDIR. Environment.apply scopes only TMPDIR and retains the original published-dependency loader environment used by the controller/plugins. Keep cleanup and all upstream tests.
ci_tmpdir_evidence:     dssi-w3-20261012-hmdfs-tmp-substep-r2 official W3 CI exit0, upstream1/1, installed consumer1/1, 12 phases and release/postrelease PASS; log SHA256217916e1725afb6847438ea5b7b0d0e92ee4dab5d78865e6128e7133984d85c7. Old CI fork failure remains infrastructure, not relabelled as a tempdir failure.
ci_reproducibility_increment: A release's generated configure does not need an ambient Automake executable merely to refresh config helpers. When its old canonicalizer is extended for compiler-proven linux-ohos, a three-part tuple strips to the bare CPU while a four-part tuple preserves CPU-vendor; both machine branches must accept aarch64.
ci_increment_scope:     Generated Autotools releases with old config.sub and an OHOS compiler-proven tuple; not projects requiring autoreconf or non-OHOS hosts.
ci_increment_boundary:  Verify bundled hashes and task backup first; narrowly extend CPU and OS cases; reject malformed/non-OHOS compiler output or canonicalizer drift; do not substitute a made-up Linux build/host tuple or change the upstream test denominator.
ci_increment_evidence:  PR14655 HEADc680d47e79d14dd23e69558a6fe3a305b6880d88 CI80114 automake executable missing; local actual-helper positive/non-OHOS/hash-drift checks3/3 plus four-part tuple accepted; W3 dssi-repair-w3-20261010T101340Z canonical aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos, upstream1/1 consumer1/1, 12 receipt release validation PASS; raw log SHA256892a57d171d130d075480f74be33b713142c6566462f429591c793d5707cf3d6.
